{"id":"o-capefairmarina-com","title":"Cape Fair Boat Dock & Marina","cat":"water","art":"pontoon","area":"Cape Fair, MO","metroId":"","src":"capefairmarina.com","rating":4.8,"reviews":717,"specs":["Located on the James River arm of Table Rock Lake","Full-service marina with food, fuel, tackle, bait, and supplies"],"options":[{"name":"Boat Rentals","detail":"","price":null},{"name":"Fishing Reports","detail":"","price":null},{"name":"Boat Rentals","detail":"Ski boats, fishing boats, pontoon boats, tubes, skis and more","price":null},{"name":"Slip Rentals","detail":"Covered slips for most any size boat and locked docks","price":null}],"services":[{"name":"Boat Rentals","desc":"Book your Table Rock Lake boat rental at Cape Fair Marina. All watercraft rentals include life jackets for every person on board. For tubes, skis, and boards add $30 to the boat rental. It's $40 to rent tubes, skis, or boards without a boat rental. Must be 21 to rent a boat. Driver(s) must be born before 1/1/1984 or show proof of boater's safety certificate. IMPORTANT: Upon arrival at the corps park, stop at the guard shack and tell them you are going to the marina store to avoid being charged. If you plan to launch a boat or use the park facilities, then you are subject to a small charge at the","photo":"data:image/png;base64,","variants":[{"label":"Standard","price":null,"optionIdx":0},{"label":"Ski boats, fishing boats, pontoon boats, tubes, skis and more","price":null,"optionIdx":2}]},{"name":"Fishing Reports","desc":"Bass fishing in the James River has started producing some really nice size fish. In fact, a friend (who is a professional guide on Table Rock Lake) Glenn Rosser reported that he had some good limits on his recent trips. His fish were caught between three and eighteen feet of water, in the two to four pound class. There are a few different patterns currently working in the river. One is an early pattern, sometimes during the early morning fog in shallow water, 2 to 5 feet on flats and secondary points in creeks and larger coves where shad are active. These fish are being caught on shallow crank baits Strike King Square Bill, KVD 1.5 or 2.5 in natural shad colors, depending on the size of","photo":"data:image/png;base64,","variants":[{"label":"Standard","price":null,"optionIdx":1}]},{"name":"Slip Rentals","desc":null,"variants":[{"label":"Covered slips for most any size boat and locked docks","price":null,"optionIdx":3}]}],"includes":["Boat rental gear included"],"addons":[],"gap":"Prices for rentals not stated","blurb":"Guests can rent ski boats, fishing boats, pontoon boats, tubes, skis and more for a day on Table Rock Lake. The marina offers covered slips for most boat sizes and a ship store with food, fuel, tackle, and bait. Dining options include Pizza World and an ice cream and coffee shop on site.","cover":"https://capefairmarina.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/08/Cape-Fair-Marina-Boat-Rental-Slip-Rental_1200x675.jpg","photos":["https://capefairmarina.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/08/Cape-Fair-Marina-Boat-Rental-Slip-Rental_1200x675.jpg"],"ytVideos":[],"lat":36.7212028,"lon":-93.5321731,"tags":["Boat rental service","Boat Rentals","Fishing Reports","Slip Rentals"],"highlights":["Located on the James River arm of Table Rock Lake","Full-service marina with food, fuel, tackle, bait, and supplies"],"requirements":[],"groupInfo":[],"bring":[],"policies":[],"hoursText":["Open Daily 8am-8pm"],"faq":[],"contact":{"domain":"capefairmarina.com","phone":"+14175384163","street":"1500 76-82","city":"Cape Fair","region":"MO","postal":"65624","hours":["Friday-Sunday 9am-7pm"]}}